     Active(5L)            OS-9 (News)            Active(5L)     NNAAMMEE                  Active   -   List   of   existing  newsgroups  with         indicies.       DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN                     This file   contains  a  list  of  all  existing         newsgroup  on  the  local installation. The file is         in  general  managed  via  ccoonnttrroollmmeessssaaggeess  but for         some  reasons you may edit it. It must be sorted to         ensure  that  news works properly. the format is in         general             <group> <last> <first> n<flag> [<sizelimit>]         for non moderated groups,      <group> <last> <first> y<flag> [<sizelimit>] [<moderator(s)>]         for moderated groups and             <group> <last> <first> r<flag> [<sizelimit>]         for  read-only  groups where <<ggrroouupp>> is the name of         the  newsgroup in lowercase letters, <<ffiirrsstt>> is the         first  (oldest)  avaiable article and <<llaasstt>> is the         last  <newest>  avaiable  article.  The newsarticel         are  stored with a filename of a number. The <<ffllaagg>>         may  be  either  uu or ii to tell that this newsgroup         is  uused  or iignored.  If a group is moderated then         the  moderator(s)  should  be  inserted after the yy         flag  with  their full mail address.  If there is a         number  after  the flags only articles with less or         equal in size of kBytes will be stored.       Page 1                            Printed (22 Dec 1992)